  "17x is NOT the code. The probe path (datalog-query-plan calling arrangement.query/query per clause) is UNCHANGED between these two runs, and it got 3.66x faster on its own -- the [?f1 knows ?f2] probe went 3859.7 -> 1071.3 ms for the same 361,246 rows. That is the host: the baseline ran at load average 150-190, this run at 40-80. Dividing through, roughly 17.04 / 3.66 = ~4.7x is attributable to the change. The unchanged probe path is the control, and it says the raw ratio is inflated about fourfold."
  :honest-summary "The two-hop join is ~4.7x faster after batching, not 17x. Row counts are identical (6,733) so nothing was traded for it."}
